 "lines": [
  {
   "start": 0.5,
   "end": 5.131,
   "text": "As they came near Jerusalem, Jesus sent two of his disciples ahead.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 5.431,
   "end": 13.352,
   "text": "Go into the village. You will find a young donkey tied there, that no one has ever ridden. Untie it, and bring it here.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 13.752,
   "end": 18.63,
   "text": "They brought the donkey to Jesus, threw their cloaks over it, and he sat on it.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 18.93,
   "end": 24.521,
   "text": "Many spread their cloaks on the road, and others spread branches they had cut in the fields.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 24.821,
   "end": 27.596,
   "text": "Hosanna! Blessed is he who comes in the name of the Lord!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 28.396,
   "end": 35.077,
   "text": "The next day, Jesus was hungry. He saw a fig tree in leaf, but found nothing on it, only leaves.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 35.477,
   "end": 38.147,
   "text": "May no one ever eat fruit from you again.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 38.747,
   "end": 44.363,
   "text": "In Jerusalem, Jesus entered the temple. It was full of people buying and selling.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 44.663,
   "end": 50.294,
   "text": "He overturned the tables of the money changers, and the benches of those selling doves.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 50.994,
   "end": 58.658,
   "text": "Is it not written: My house will be called a house of prayer for all nations? But you have made it a den of robbers!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 59.258,
   "end": 66.578,
   "text": "The chief priests heard this, and began looking for a way to kill him. For the whole crowd was amazed at his teaching.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 67.078,
   "end": 71.814,
   "text": "The next morning, they passed the fig tree. It had withered, from the roots.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 72.114,
   "end": 74.625,
   "text": "Teacher, look! The fig tree you cursed has withered!",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 75.025,
   "end": 83.944,
   "text": "Have faith in God. If anyone says to this mountain: Go, throw yourself into the sea, and does not doubt, it will be done.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 84.544,
   "end": 90.422,
   "text": "Whatever you ask for in prayer, believe that you have received it, and it will be yours.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 90.922,
   "end": 96.009,
   "text": "And when you stand praying, if you hold anything against anyone, forgive them.",
   "tempter": false
  },
  {
   "start": 96.909,
   "end": 100.333,
   "text": "Follow for part sixteen.",
   "tempter": false
  }
 ]
}